# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Jinxed Leviathan), edited. The Jinxed Leviathan: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_leviathan_arrived
Narrator: Murkwater Bend, stilt shacks and swamplights, boats sunk at their moorings, and a stink of old luck gone sour.
check Wisdom DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You follow your own lantern and the swamplights lose their pull.
set mf_leviathan_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: The swamplights lure a hero off the boardwalk, and they come back damp and muddled.
damage 3d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk the boardwalk, and every third plank gives way, and the swamplights wink knowingly.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: She says everything in the bayou has been going wrong this week: the boats sink, the dice fall badly, and something huge turns in the water at night.
set mf_leviathan_asked
quest mf_leviathan asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: She says another punt sank on a calm morning, and asks what you have learned.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_leviathan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_nadine_bayou [weary]: Everything goes wrong by a little, always, swamplights lead folk astray, and the party-goers dance until they drop.
-> menu

~ where
mf_nadine_bayou [sad]: She says an alligator was hexed into a colossus of bad luck to fight Snake Eye Jack, and it ate its makers, and it is in the bayou's deep pool.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_nadine_bayou [neutral]: She says a giant serpent sacred to Jack's followers nests upstream; the Leviathan hates it, and might follow you if you used it.
* [Animal Handling DC 19] Bait the Leviathan with the sacred serpent -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Survival DC 19] Read the serpent's nesting place to lead the Leviathan -> a_ok | a_slow
* Drag bait through the swamp and see what follows -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_nadine_bayou [smile]: The great serpent drifts through the water, and the Leviathan turns slowly, drawn after it toward its pool.
time +60
set mf_leviathan_found
set mf_leviathan_clue_a
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: It takes a long wet afternoon of luring and bad luck, but the Leviathan finally turns toward the pool.
time +300
set mf_leviathan_found
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_jack_follower [smile]: He tips his hat and says it is a fine day for tempting fate, and would you like a drink to your health.
set mf_leviathan_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_jack_follower [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_leviathan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_leviathan_found and not flag.mf_leviathan_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_jack_follower [smile]: He says the followers bless idols of Jack for luck, and that a blessed idol rebounds a curse, which would be very bad news for a Leviathan.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_jack_follower [sly]: He says he knows where the beast was made, and might tell you for a fair bargain or a fair threat.
* [Intimidation DC 19] Intimidate him into telling where it was made -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Persuasion DC 19] Charm him into telling where it was made -> b_ok | b_slow
* Let him talk and listen to every wandering tale -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_jack_follower [sly]: He tells you the whole sorry story, the hexing and the sinking, and where the pool is.
time +60
set mf_leviathan_found
set mf_leviathan_clue_b
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It takes a long drunken afternoon of rambling, but in the end he tells where the pool is.
time +300
set mf_leviathan_found
quest mf_leviathan trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_jack_follower [smile]: He says you need an idol of Snake Eye Jack blessed by a true follower; and he happens to be one.
* [Religion DC 19] Persuade him to bless an idol for you -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Persuasion DC 19] Show proper reverence so he blesses it freely -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Pay your respects at the shrine and ask politely, over hours -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_jack_follower [smile]: He lays a small idol in your hands and murmurs a blessing, and for a moment the whole swamp seems to wink.
time +60
give mf_blessed_idol
set mf_leviathan_weak
quest mf_leviathan ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of dutiful respect at the shrine, but he finally blesses the idol.
time +300
give mf_blessed_idol
set mf_leviathan_weak
quest mf_leviathan ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The boardwalk ends at a cursed pool, black and still, with an island of mud and bones in its middle.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_leviathan_reveals
Narrator: The Jinxed Leviathan breaks the surface of the pool, a colossal alligator with a crown of old hexes, grinning.
cutscene mf_leviathan_reveals_2
Narrator: Its mouth opens, and the air fills with sour luck.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_leviathan_weak
combat mf_leviathan_weak
elif level >= 18
combat mf_leviathan_full
else
combat mf_leviathan_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_leviathan_falls
Narrator: The Leviathan sinks beneath the pool, finally unlucky, and the swamplights wink out one by one.
cutscene mf_leviathan_falls_2
Narrator: The moon turns its gaze south and west, toward a forest of spiders.
cutscene end
set mf_leviathan_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give tooth_of_the_jinxed_leviathan
quest mf_leviathan slain
xp milestone
Narrator: In the Webwoods something is stitching, and children have stopped playing.
-> END
